     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Data minimization</h2>
+    <p>We collect only what is needed to operate the site. Reading articles requires no account. Your reading list is stored in a server-side session identified by a single functional cookie; it contains only article identifiers, is capped in size, and is never used for profiling. We do not store IP addresses or personal profiles in the application.</p>
+
+    <h2>5. Third parties</h2>
+    <p>We keep third-party integrations to a minimum and list them here:</p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Account service</strong> (us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net): receives the username and password you submit when signing up or in. Requests are sent without cookies or referrer information.</li>
+        <li><strong>Analytics script</strong> (same host): loaded <em>only</em> after you click “Accept analytics”. It is never loaded if your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signals. You can change your choice at any time via “Manage Privacy Preferences” in the footer.</li>
+        <li><strong>Fonts</strong>: served from our own system font stack; no font provider is contacted.</li>
+        <li><strong>Advertising</strong>: currently disabled; no ad network scripts are loaded.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>Third-party integrations are reviewed before being added and audited periodically, including the origins permitted by our Content Security Policy.</p>
+
+    <h2>6. Security</h2>
+    <p>The site is served over HTTPS only (HSTS) with a strict Content Security Policy, framing protection, and restrictive browser permission policies. API responses are never cached.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
